I would re-word the first one to be a bit more emphatic --
*Nethack is a turn-based game*.

People who treat nethack as if it were chess, and think one move or
even several ahead, will prosper. Those who treat it as if it were a
twitch -- reflex -- game are fated to never ascend.

Some other commandments:

"Thou shalt use a wand of teleport as a wand of death".
It isn't really, but against any monster not able to teleport it will
buy you much valuable time. It works equally well on monsters that
aren't effected by death.

"Thou shalt never read a scroll, drink a potion, wear an amulet or
ring, or zap a wand that is completely unidentified".

This game became a lot easier when I stopped taking those kinds of
chances.

Here's another one:

"Thou shalt never pick up a scroll in a shop unless you have at least
200 gold on your person".

Reason: It's possible that scroll is cursed scare monster.  You touch
it -- it turns to dust. You owe the shopkeeper around 200 gold. If
you're a level 3 character, there's a good chance you'll be trapped in
the shop.  Even if you tunnel out or teleport, you still have to deal
with the cops. NOT a good thing, if you're not prepared for it.

"Thou shalt use wands of digging to engrave "E", and scrolls of
teleport to escape without hesitation and at the slightest
provocation".

Both exist in the dungeon in large quantities for a reason.

